\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. Cradled in a manger, meanly
\par Laid the Son of Man His head;
\par Sleeping His first earthly slumber
\par Where the oxen had been fed.
\par Happy were those shepherds listening
\par To the holy angel's word;
\par Happy they within that stable,
\par Worshipping their infant Lord.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Happy all who hear the message
\par Of His coming from above;
\par Happier still who hail His coming,
\par And with praises greet His Love.
\par Blessed Saviour, Christ most holy,
\par In a manger Thou didst rest;
\par Canst Thou stoop again, yet lower,
\par And abide within my breast?
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. Evil things are there before Thee;
\par In the heart, where they have fed,
\par Wilt Thou pitifully enter,
\par Son of Man, and lay Thy head?
\par Enter, then, O Christ most holy;
\par Make a Christmas in my heart;
\par Make a heaven of my manger:
\par It is heaven where Thou art.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. And to those who never listened
\par To the messenge of Thy birth,
\par Who have winter, but no Christmas
\par Bringing them Thy peace on earth,
\par Send to these the joyful tidings;
\par By all people, in each home,
\par Be there heard the Christmas anthem:
\par Praise to God, the Christ has come!\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

